      "dom_id": "question-64028",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose fourth term is $8$ and whose seventh term is $216.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{7}=216$ and ${a}_{4}=8.$ Substituting $n=7$ and $m=4$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-4} & =\\frac{{a}_{7}}{{a}_{4}} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{216}{8} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3} & =27 \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={3}^{3} \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
