      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose sixth term is $-15$ and whose ninth term is $-\\frac{3}{25}.$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{9}=-\\frac{3}{25}$ and ${a}_{6}=-15.$ Substituting $n=9$ and $m=6$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{9-6} & =\\frac{{a}_{9}}{{a}_{6}} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{25})}{(-15)} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{125} \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
